                  "page_end": 6,
                  "page_start": 6,
                  "paraphrased": false,
                  "text_excerpt": "This suggests that the dose of many HDAC inhibitors governs the magnitude of a cell's response rather than its rate of progression"
                },
                "statement": "The dose of many HDAC inhibitors governs the magnitude of a cell's response rather than the rate of progression."
              },
              {
                "additional_provenance": [],
                "claim_id": "clm_1ded39a74681eb17b0d72d42",
                "inference_basis_ids": [
                  "res_3afe2b95d5b709e3ed3cde9f"
                ],
                "polarity": "positive",
                "provenance": {
                  "chunk_id": "ec1a581fca4642833f76",
                  "page_end": 7,
                  "page_start": 7,
                  "paraphrased": false,
                  "text_excerpt": "In both A549 and MCF7 cells, acetate, pyruvate, and citrate supplementation was capable of blocking pracinostat-treated cells from reaching the end of the HDAC inhibitor trajectory"
                },
                "statement": "Exogenous acetate, pyruvate, or citrate can partially rescue cells from HDAC inhibitor-induced transcriptional trajectory, supporting the acetyl-CoA depletion model."
              },
              {
                "additional_provenance": [],
                "claim_id": "clm_71d3394c1cfa66e7f704190b",
                "inference_basis_ids": [],
                "polarity": "positive",
                "provenance": {
                  "chunk_id": "a7af132d732a56a324bc",
                  "page_end": 6,
                  "page_start": 6,
                  "paraphrased": false,
                  "text_excerpt": "With the exception of two relatively insoluble compounds, our calculated TC50 values increased as a function of compound IC50 values"
                },
                "statement": "sci-Plex-derived TC50 values for HDAC inhibitors correlate with published biochemical IC50 values."
              },
              {
                "additional_provenance": [],
                "claim_id": "clm_faab26d6aa9ae75dbc7d242b",
                "inference_basis_ids": [
                  "res_6adebf5594b5e35ca46bcd19",
                  "res_895cb1140a3f5389460d2de9"
                ],
                "polarity": "positive",
                "provenance": {
                  "chunk_id": "ec1a581fca4642833f76",
                  "page_end": 7,
                  "page_start": 7,
                  "paraphrased": false,
                  "text_excerpt": "we observed that enzymes critical for cytoplasmic acetyl-CoA synthesis from either citrate (ACLY) or acetate (ACSS2) were up-regulated"
                },
                "statement": "HDAC inhibitors induce a transcriptional response consistent with acetyl-CoA depletion, including upregulation of ACSS2, ACLY, and genes involved in citrate metabolism."
              }
            ],
            "datasets": [],
            "evidence_spans": [],
            "experiments_or_tasks": [
              "Analysis of HDAC inhibitor response across three cell lines, including trajectory alignment and validation with metabolite supplementation and enzyme inhibition"
            ],
            "methods": [
              {
                "method_id": "m_4",
                "name": "HDAC inhibitor trajectory analysis",
                "protocol_description": "MNN alignment of HDAC-treated cells from three cell lines to create a consensus pseudodose trajectory; differential expression along pseudodose."
              },
              {
                "method_id": "m_5",
                "name": "Metabolite supplementation experiment",
                "protocol_description": "A549 and MCF7 cells treated with pracinostat plus acetyl-CoA precursors (acetate, pyruvate, citrate) or inhibitors of acetyl-CoA synthesis enzymes (ACLY, ACSS2, PDH) for 24 hours, then processed by sci-Plex."
              }
            ],
            "name": "HDAC inhibitor mechanism-of-action analysis",
            "results": [
              {
                "additional_provenance": [],
                "metric_name": "Effect of metabolite supplementation on HDAC inhibitor trajectory",
                "n_sample_size": null,
                "p_value": null,
                "provenance": {
                  "chunk_id": "ec1a581fca4642833f76",
                  "page_end": 7,
                  "page_start": 7,
                  "paraphrased": false,
                  "text_excerpt": "In both A549 and MCF7 cells, acetate, pyruvate, and citrate supplementation was capable of blocking pracinostat-treated cells from reaching the end of the HDAC inhibitor trajectory"
                },
                "quantitative_value": null,
                "result_id": "res_3afe2b95d5b709e3ed3cde9f",
                "unit": null,
                "value_raw_text": "Acetate, pyruvate, and citrate supplementation blocked pracinostat-treated cells from reaching the end of the HDAC inhibitor trajectory in both A549 and MCF7"
              },
              {
                "additional_provenance": [],
                "metric_name": "Number of differentially expressed genes along HDAC inhibitor trajectory",
                "n_sample_size": null,
                "p_value": null,
                "provenance": {
                  "chunk_id": "a7af132d732a56a324bc",
                  "page_end": 6,
                  "page_start": 6,
                  "paraphrased": false,
                  "text_excerpt": "Of the 4308 genes that were significantly differentially expressed over this consensus trajectory, 2081 (48%) responded in a cell-type–dependent manner and 942 (22%) exhibited the same pattern in all three cell lines"
                },
                "quantitative_value": 4308.0,
                "result_id": "res_6adebf5594b5e35ca46bcd19",
                "unit": null,
                "value_raw_text": "4308 genes significantly differentially expressed; 2081 cell-type-dependent, 942 shared across cell lines"
              },
              {
                "additional_provenance": [],
                "metric_name": "Acetylated lysine levels",
                "n_sample_size": null,
                "p_value": null,
                "provenance": {
                  "chunk_id": "ec1a581fca4642833f76",
                  "page_end": 7,
                  "page_start": 7,
                  "paraphrased": false,
                  "text_excerpt": "we observed that HDAC inhibition led to sequestration of acetate in the form of markedly increased acetylated lysine levels after exposure to a 10 μM dose of the HDAC inhibitors pracinostat and abexinostat"
                },
                "quantitative_value": null,
                "result_id": "res_895cb1140a3f5389460d2de9",
                "unit": null,
                "value_raw_text": "markedly increased acetylated lysine levels after exposure to 10 μM pracinostat or abexinostat"
              },
              {
                "additional_provenance": [],
                "metric_name": "G2/M accumulation by flow cytometry",
                "n_sample_size": null,
                "p_value": null,
                "provenance": {
